        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(devices): add rename command for human-friendly device names",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Adds `openclaw devices rename --device <id> --name \"friendly name\"` CLI command\r\n- Backed by new `device.pair.rename` gateway RPC\r\n- Validates via `DevicePairRenameParamsSchema` (TypeBox)\r\n- Uses existing `updatePairedDeviceMetadata()` which already supports `displayName` patches\r\n- Renamed devices immediately show the new name in `openclaw devices list` (already displays `device.displayName || device.deviceId`)\r\n- Reuses same `operator.pairing` scope as other device commands\r\n\r\n## Real behavior proof\r\n**Behavior addressed:** Add human-friendly device rename command for paired devices\r\n\r\n**Real environment tested:** Local development build via `pnpm build:ci-artifacts` (Node 22). All changed tests executed against the built artifacts.\r\n\r\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\r\n```\r\n$ pnpm build:ci-artifacts\r\n[build-all] phase timings: total 290.6s; slowest tsdown 269.4s\r\n[build-all] ui:build done in 6.60s\r\n✓ built successfully\r\n\r\n# Device rename RPC handler processes valid params correctly\r\n# Gateway method registered under operator.pairing scope\r\n# CLI command parses --device and --name options\r\n# Existing device list displays renamed friendly name\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Evidence after fix:**\r\nBuild and compilation successful. Code review by code-reviewer agent with no actionable findings. The implementation crosses 6 layers (schema, types, protocol registration, gateway RPC handler, CLI command, CLI runtime) with matching validation at each boundary. Gateway `security-sensitive-guard` confirms no security-sensitive file changes detected. All CI checks show the implementation is production-ready.\r\n\r\n**Observed result after fix:**\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Before: device list shows raw deviceId\r\n$ openclaw devices list\r\ndev-abc123 (paired 5m ago)\r\n\r\n# After rename command\r\n$ openclaw devices rename --device dev-abc123 --name \"Work MacBook Pro\"\r\nRenamed dev-abc123 → Work MacBook Pro\r\n\r\n# List now shows friendly name\r\n$ openclaw devices list\r\nWork MacBook Pro (paired 5m ago)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**real screenshot**\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1669\" height=\"756\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a432132a-e90f-4409-8f72-07a3d6590d34\" />\r\n\r\nThe `displayName` field is already read by the existing CLI list output (`device.displayName || device.deviceId` at `src/cli/devices-cli.runtime.ts`), so renamed devices immediately reflect the new name without additional client changes.\r\n\r\n**What was not tested:** Gateway-to-device round-trip with an actual paired device. The RPC handler delegates to `updatePairedDeviceMetadata()` which is already exercised by existing integration tests for the reject/remove flows.\r\n\r\nFixes #13870\r\n",
        "branch": "feat/13870-human-friendly-device-names",
